    "The proposed use of the dwellinghouse as a supported living accommodation facility for up to 5 persons (5 bed) (Use Class C3(b)) would not result in a material change of use from Class C3 (Dwellinghouses) and would therefore be within the tolerances of the Town and Country Planning (Use Class) Order 1987 (as amended).The proposal is therefore a lawful development."
